---
import { Camera, Code2, Compass, MapPin, Search } from 'lucide-astro';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head><BaseHead title="About | Brian Monroe" description="Thirty years online, from Netscape and GeoCities to building thoughtful digital experiences today." /></head>
	<body class="site-page">
		<Header />
		<main>
			<PageHero eyebrow="About / 30 years online" title="I didn’t just learn the web. I grew up with it." description="My first browser was Netscape Navigator. I built GeoCities sites in middle school. I’ve had a front-row seat as the internet became the place where we work, create, connect, and live." />
			<section class="content-section">
				<div class="site-shell about-grid">
					<div class="prose-dark story">
						<p>I’ve been on the internet for about 30 years—not only developing for it, but watching it become what it is today.</p>
						<p>I was there for the strange, creative early web, when making a GeoCities page meant teaching yourself how the whole thing worked. I watched Napster and LimeWire change how people found and shared culture. I studied Adobe Flash and ActionScript, only to watch browsers eventually close the door on the entire platform.</p>
						<p>I found WordPress around 2010, when it still felt like a refreshingly simple way to give people control of their own websites. I was also using social media before there were Business Pages, content calendars, or “influencers”—back when it felt more like a place people went than a channel brands had to manage.</p>
						<p>That history gave me something more useful than nostalgia: perspective. Technologies come and go. Good communication, curiosity, adaptability, and respect for the person on the other side of the screen keep mattering.</p>
						<p>Today I bring that perspective to websites, search strategy, photography, content, and digital design for businesses and organizations that want a clearer presence online.</p>
						<a class="site-button" href="/#contact-form">Start a conversation</a>
					</div>
					<div class="about-side">
						<aside class="glass-panel experience-card">
							<div class="experience-stat">
								<span>30</span>
								<div><strong>years online</strong><small>and still curious about what comes next.</small></div>
							</div>
						</aside>
						<aside class="glass-panel about-card">
							<p class="about-label">A very abbreviated history</p>
							<ul class="timeline">
								<li><span>1990s</span><div><strong>Netscape Navigator</strong><small>My first window into the web</small></div></li>
								<li><span>1990s</span><div><strong>GeoCities</strong><small>Building websites in middle school</small></div></li>
								<li><span>2000s</span><div><strong>Napster & LimeWire</strong><small>Watching the internet reshape culture</small></div></li>
								<li><span>2000s</span><div><strong>Flash & ActionScript</strong><small>Learning a platform—and how quickly platforms change</small></div></li>
								<li><span>2000s</span><div><strong>Social media</strong><small>Before Business Pages, algorithms, and influencers</small></div></li>
								<li><span>~2010</span><div><strong>WordPress</strong><small>Discovering a simple CMS that put publishing within reach</small></div></li>
								<li><span>Now</span><div><strong>The open web</strong><small>Still building, learning, and adapting</small></div></li>
							</ul>
						</aside>
						<aside class="glass-panel about-card">
							<p class="about-label">Working across</p>
							<ul>
								<li><Code2 size={18} /> Web development</li>
								<li><Search size={18} /> Search & analytics</li>
								<li><Camera size={18} /> Photography & content</li>
								<li><Compass size={18} /> Digital strategy</li>
								<li><MapPin size={18} /> Celina, Ohio</li>
							</ul>
						</aside>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.about-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 56px; align-items: start; }
	.prose-dark { margin: 0; }
	.prose-dark p:first-child { margin-top: 0; color: #eef0ec; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.55; }
	.story p { margin: 0 0 24px; }
	.prose-dark .site-button { margin-top: 18px; text-decoration: none; color: white; }
	.about-side { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
	.experience-card { padding: 28px 30px; }
	.experience-stat { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: center; gap: 22px; }
	.experience-stat > span { color: #e87338; font-size: 68px; font-weight: 500; line-height: .85; letter-spacing: -.06em; }
	.experience-stat > div { display: grid; gap: 3px; }
	.experience-stat strong { color: #eef0ec; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.2; }
	.experience-stat small { color: #969c95; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4; }
	.about-card { padding: 30px; }
	.about-label { margin: 0 0 22px; color: #858b84; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
	.about-card ul { display: grid; gap: 0; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
	.about-card li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; padding: 17px 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09); color: #b5bab3; font-size: 15px; }
	.about-card svg { color: #e87338; }
	.about-card .timeline { gap: 0; }
	.about-card .timeline li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 54px minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: start; gap: 16px; padding: 18px 0; }
	.timeline > li > span { padding-top: 3px; color: #e87338; font: 10px/1.4 ui-monospace, monospace; text-transform: uppercase; }
	.timeline div { display: grid; gap: 3px; }
	.timeline strong { color: #d9dcd7; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.3; }
	.timeline small { color: #858b84; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.45; }
	@media(max-width: 800px) { .about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 48px; } }
</style>
